    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Spanish Civil War, the Dehesa of Navalcarbón in Las Rozas still bears concrete bunkers from the 1936 battles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Las_Rozas_de_Madrid"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1960s, Samuel Bronston built a luxurious studio near Las Matas, and the town hosted the filming of 55 Days at Peking with local extras.",
